		"Mechanism: prompts.submit appends the inbox record, then sets running.interrupt and aborts running.controller (turns.ts sits at the 400-line limit). runTurn's loop top sees the aborted signal: with interrupt set it makes a new AbortController and re-requests (the inbox is delivered before every request); without it (Escape/close via turns.stop, which clears interrupt) it ends paused. Pending tool calls get an error result so replay stays paired. Also resolves a submit right after Escape while the turn still settles: the turn resumes with the message instead of pausing."
